s blood was  allegedly tainted and inferior to the  blood of other humans and as he recalls  these tragic memories Shoji is able to  summon more strength and he then manages  to break away from the villains who had  been holding him down during the  struggle his face mask falls off and his  real face is finally revealed we also  see that he has multiple scars on his  face probably as a direct result of all  the oppression and abuse that he had  faced as a child and yet Shoji isn't  angry about the abuse that he suffered  he is angry that these villains who  claim to speak for him and who claim to  represent people like him are out here  preparing to storm a hospital and harm  countless innocent people for their  so-called cause joji proclaims that if  they intend to attack this hospital  without even evacuating the people  inside it he will never forgive them and  that is how this chapter ends even  though this chapter took us away from  the main battles and the main characters  I actually thought that it was a great  chapter it gave us some serious World  building and even though some of this  stuff was definitely hinted at before I  actually wish that it had been explored  more by this point in the story this is  clearly very important stuff that still  has serious consequences in the world of  mha and this type of discrimination  against people who just happen to look  different is clearly a direct parallel  to racism in our own world there is a  powerful message here and Shoji's  experience as someone who faced  oppression and then still decided to  become a hero is extremely interesting I  honestly wish that we got to see more of  this and learn more about him earlier on  because it's great stuff Shoji is  usually one of the characters you don't  really think too much much about in  class 1a and yet in reality he is so  interesting oh and I know that horikoshi  loves his Star Wars references but I  don't think that he needed to break our  immersion during such 